    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d281">

                <pb facs="0363" n="345" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg345"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.00/6–1446: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Adam</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-06-15T18:00:00-04:00">June 15, 1946—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>330. Urtel no. 535. Explaining that he was speaking personally and as genuine
                    friend Bolivia Assistant Secretary Braden expressed to Ambassador Andrade this
                    afternoon his alarm recent developments as reported by you. After summarizing
                    information contained your recent tels and concern apparent possibility
                    executions following mass arrests, Braden described violation chancery premises
                    June 13 and attempt following night. He said you had been instructed to submit
                    note of protest and indicated contents thereof.</p>
                <p>Ambassador replied without recent information developments in <pb facs="0364"
                        n="346" xml:id="pg346"/> capital but desired express in own name and Govt’s
                    profound regret invasion Embassy together with assurances he would immediately
                    telegraph La Paz full report conversation.</p>
                <p>Braden then mentioned Belmonte possible return stating that obviously this is
                    matter for Bolivian Govt decide but that, again as friend of Bolivia, he felt
                    Ambassador should be aware extremely adverse effect return might have on public
                    opinion this country and on attitude here toward Bolivian Govt.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
